# GenX: hardening defaults with a measurable per-syscall/per-allocation cost
# that CachyOS inherits from Arch. Each one stays compiled in and can be
# re-enabled at boot (init_on_alloc=1, randomize_kstack_offset=on,
# hardened_usercopy=on). This machine already boots with mitigations=off,
# so the trade-off is consistent with the owner's choice. Delete this file
# to keep the CachyOS defaults.
# CONFIG_INIT_ON_ALLOC_DEFAULT_ON is not set
# CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET_DEFAULT is not set
# CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY_DEFAULT_ON is not set
